WEBVTT

01:32.040 --> 01:34.990
<b>Black Wolf Nightslayer</b>

01:52.250 --> 01:53.250
And...

01:54.510 --> 01:58.510
You're certain that Sunraku was his name?

01:58.510 --> 02:03.090
Y-Yeah... I'm pretty sure that 
was his character name...

02:05.850 --> 02:07.840
Mia! Don't do that!

02:07.840 --> 02:10.100
That's not a monster, it's a player!

02:10.100 --> 02:11.900
R-Really?

02:11.900 --> 02:14.090
But it's really scary-looking...

02:15.350 --> 02:17.730
Scary-looking players are still players!

02:18.970 --> 02:23.590
So, this player named "Sunraku." 
Do you know where he ha—

02:23.590 --> 02:24.920
Er, where did he go?

02:24.920 --> 02:25.790
R-Right!

02:25.790 --> 02:28.450
I think he'd gotten a face full 
of poison from the Python.

02:28.450 --> 02:30.170
He ran off into Secondale!

02:31.120 --> 02:34.210
And he was half-naked, with a bird's head?

02:34.210 --> 02:37.510
Yeah, but he could've changed 
his equipment by now...

02:37.510 --> 02:40.540
The mask had such a scary expression.

02:40.540 --> 02:41.970
I thought it was a monster!

02:43.020 --> 02:45.200
<i>I almost didn't believe it,</i>

02:45.200 --> 02:49.720
<i>but he really beat the Ravenous Python 
without visiting the first town...</i>

02:50.100 --> 02:51.960
Thank you for the information.

02:51.960 --> 02:54.010
As an expression of my gratitude...

02:56.270 --> 02:57.170
Take it.

02:56.880 --> 02:57.740
<b>Gift</b>

02:56.880 --> 02:57.740
<b>Coordinate Teleporter</b>

03:00.150 --> 03:02.740
Th-Thanks.

03:02.740 --> 03:03.760
Now...

03:04.610 --> 03:05.490
I'm in a hurry. Goodbye.

03:14.280 --> 03:15.650
So fast!

03:15.650 --> 03:17.390
Who was that?

03:17.390 --> 03:20.840
Not sure, but the emblem on the cape...

03:21.410 --> 03:25.350
I think it's from a clan focused on that 
unique monster, Lycagon the Nightslayer.

03:25.590 --> 03:27.400
Unique monster?

03:27.760 --> 03:28.970
Lycagon?

03:28.970 --> 03:32.970
Unique monsters are a 
special class of monsters

03:32.970 --> 03:35.050
with both an individual name and a title.

03:36.070 --> 03:39.740
Most monsters, when you beat them 
or capture them or whatever,

03:39.740 --> 03:43.360
respawn as a new individual after 
a set period of time passes.

03:43.360 --> 03:47.880
But for the unique monsters, there's 
only one of each in the whole world.

03:49.350 --> 04:00.760
<b>The Seven Colossi</b>

03:49.460 --> 03:53.880
Rumor says there's seven of them in <i>SLF</i>,

03:53.880 --> 03:57.430
but we don't even know the spawn 
criteria for most of them.

03:57.850 --> 04:00.760
For each of these unique 
monsters, called "Colossi,"

04:00.990 --> 04:06.020
lots of top players have formed 
clans focused on taking them out.

04:08.090 --> 04:09.010
Wow...

04:09.280 --> 04:11.790
So they're just really rare monsters?

04:11.790 --> 04:14.470
That's about what it boils down to, yeah.

04:14.470 --> 04:18.020
The issue is how abnormally strong they are.

04:18.310 --> 04:21.420
See, it's been a year since the game started,

04:21.420 --> 04:24.440
but even with a playerbase 
of over 30 million,

04:24.440 --> 04:28.480
not one person has defeated 
a single unique monster.

04:36.540 --> 04:40.900
<b>Unique Monster
Lycagon the Nightslayer
 Encountered</b>

04:36.710 --> 04:40.450
<i>Unique monster, Lycagon the
Nightslayer, encountered.</i>

04:41.530 --> 04:44.680
Unique... monster?

05:00.080 --> 05:02.640
<i>As damn tough as those Redcaps were...</i>

05:04.670 --> 05:06.740
<i>it blew 'em away in a second.</i>

05:07.790 --> 05:10.200
<i>One hit from that and I'm a goner, I'll bet.</i>

05:32.020 --> 05:32.890
You...

05:53.420 --> 05:57.010
You unique monsters don't have 
much going for you, do you?!

05:57.010 --> 05:59.930
<i>Th-That was freaking close!</i>

06:01.940 --> 06:05.760
<i>I'm so glad I spent all night grinding!</i>

06:06.240 --> 06:09.720
<i>If I hadn't learned Perfect Parry, 
I'd be totally dead right now!</i>

06:07.510 --> 06:09.720
<b>Perfect Parry
</b>Able to parry an enemy's physical attack
if executed with exact timing.

06:14.350 --> 06:17.100
<i>One second's lapse and I'm done for!</i>

06:18.010 --> 06:19.600
Better go all-out!

06:20.250 --> 06:21.000
<b>Vorpal Choppers
</b>Equipped

06:23.500 --> 06:24.250
<b>Slide Step
</b>Bonus to user's evasion.

06:34.570 --> 06:36.100
How'd you like that, huh?!

07:16.740 --> 07:17.750
It disappeared again?

07:19.620 --> 07:20.710
Where'll it come from next?

07:44.850 --> 07:46.270
It's teleporting?!

08:20.260 --> 08:21.100
Ribbit.

08:27.360 --> 08:28.340
<i>Damn it...</i>

08:28.340 --> 08:31.920
<i>The thing's pelt is tougher than 
the Ravenous Python's scales!</i>

08:32.320 --> 08:35.900
<i>I've been whaling on the thing for over 
five minutes without taking a hit...</i>

08:35.900 --> 08:36.910
<i>But...</i>

08:37.210 --> 08:40.390
<i>The thing's so tough, I don't think 
I'm actually doing any damage!</i>

08:40.390 --> 08:44.410
<i>Pretty sure I've landed a 
hundred... no, two hundred crits!</i>

08:45.070 --> 08:48.420
<i>My Vorpal Choppers, which started out close 
to mint, are already falling apart...</i>

08:49.220 --> 08:51.340
<i>If I don't find a softer 
spot to land a hit on,</i>

08:52.300 --> 08:54.460
<i>my weapons are gonna crap out before I do!</i>

08:54.460 --> 08:56.180
<i>Actually, I'd say...</i>

08:56.180 --> 08:59.680
<i>this thing's way out of the league 
of what I can fight right now!</i>

09:01.090 --> 09:03.180
<i>But that's the way I like it!</i>

09:03.430 --> 09:04.690
<i>That's the way!</i>

09:05.050 --> 09:08.190
<i>That's what makes it the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

09:08.520 --> 09:12.190
<i>This spine-tingling intensity that 
makes me feel like I'm on fire...</i>

09:14.620 --> 09:17.950
<i>It's not possible to enjoy 
a game more than this!</i>

09:18.240 --> 09:21.750
<i>Bugs! Garbage balance! Absurd spawn rates!</i>

09:21.750 --> 09:25.260
<i>I'm a gamer who's made it 
through all those trash games!</i>

09:28.170 --> 09:31.290
<i>And since I know <i>you</i> don't 
have a bugged-out hitbox...</i>

09:31.290 --> 09:35.210
<i>There's no way in hell I'm 
gonna throw in the towel!</i>

09:42.020 --> 09:44.680
<i>I'm too far for its attack to hit me.</i>

09:52.860 --> 09:53.710
<i>It's roaring?!</i>

09:54.470 --> 09:56.010
<i>I can't move!</i>

10:11.910 --> 10:13.880
<i>What'd it do to me?</i>

10:14.860 --> 10:16.380
<i>What'd it hit me with?</i>

10:23.060 --> 10:25.640
<i>Reality's a harsh mistress, huh?</i>

10:26.180 --> 10:29.280
<i>I'm not gonna suddenly 
learn an awesome new skill</i>

10:29.280 --> 10:33.160
<i>or get saved by a run-in from some 
mysterious high-level player...</i>

10:33.160 --> 10:36.780
<i>None of that cinematic stuff for me.</i>

10:37.690 --> 10:40.750
<i>Actually... I did get one break.</i>

10:40.750 --> 10:43.910
<i>Somehow, after a hit like that, 
I've got an HP remaining...</i>

10:41.660 --> 10:43.910
<i><b>Sunraku</b></i>

10:44.550 --> 10:45.910
<i>It's gotta be a miracle.</i>

10:51.190 --> 10:54.170
You're absurdly strong, you know that?

10:54.980 --> 10:59.580
But that absurdity was 
intentionally coded into you.

10:59.580 --> 11:03.140
You're exactly as strong as 
your creators wanted you to be.

11:03.460 --> 11:05.000
<i>In other words...</i>

11:06.080 --> 11:07.700
<i>It's a </i>beatable<i> absurdity.</i>

11:11.960 --> 11:12.990
I've made up my mind.

11:13.530 --> 11:16.220
I don't give a damn about 
the final boss or the story.

11:16.810 --> 11:18.900
It might not be now, but someday...

11:19.450 --> 11:21.790
I'm gonna beat you, for sure.

11:23.540 --> 11:26.790
You better not let anyone 
beat you before then...

11:26.790 --> 11:30.540
Lycagon the Nightslayer!

11:55.360 --> 11:58.400
<b>Lycagon's Mark (Curse)
</b>Applied

12:02.590 --> 12:05.200
<b>Respawn
Secondale  Inn</b>

12:05.450 --> 12:06.140
Huh?

12:12.570 --> 12:13.530
A curse?

12:16.210 --> 12:19.210
"Lycagon's Mark (Curse)."

12:16.210 --> 12:24.470
<b>Lycagon's Mark (Curse)
</b>Equipment cannot be equipped to the body part afflicted with Lycagon's Mark. 
 Monsters of lower level than the afflicted character will flee. 
 Conversations with NPCs will be affected by the presence of Lycagon's Mark.
 The afflicted body part gains resistance to magic effects.
 The curse can be removed through the prayers of a Saint or the defeat of the curse's caster.

12:19.580 --> 12:24.490
"Equipment cannot be equipped to the body 
part afflicted with Lycagon's Mark."

12:35.750 --> 12:36.980
Hang on.

12:38.090 --> 12:40.840
Am I... screwed?

12:44.730 --> 12:46.740
Lycagon's Mark?!

12:47.340 --> 12:49.370
What the heck is this crap?!

12:49.610 --> 12:52.620
I can't equip stuff to my torso or legs!

12:53.020 --> 12:54.810
That piece of crap wolf!

12:54.810 --> 12:56.770
It shows up out of nowhere, 
chomps me, and marks me?!

12:56.770 --> 12:58.180
With a curse?!

12:58.630 --> 13:01.630
<b>Staring Bird Mask
 Lycagon's Mark
 Splitblade Belt
 Lycagon's Mark
 None</b>

12:58.630 --> 13:02.300
You can't just destroy a 
guy's equipment like that!

13:02.300 --> 13:06.370
"Equipment cannot be equipped to the body 
part afflicted with Lycagon's Mark."

13:06.370 --> 13:10.400
"Monsters of lower level than the 
afflicted character will flee."

13:10.400 --> 13:12.560
"Conversations with NPCs will be affected 
by the presence of Lycagon's Mark."

13:12.560 --> 13:14.960
"The afflicted body part gains 
resistance to magic effects."

13:14.960 --> 13:17.900
"The curse can be removed 
through the prayers of a Saint

13:18.240 --> 13:22.900
or the defeat of the curse's caster"...

13:27.630 --> 13:32.160
The kind of curse where you gotta 
destroy the root to be rid of it, huh?

13:37.700 --> 13:39.520
Nice weather today.

13:41.340 --> 13:42.550
This...

13:42.550 --> 13:43.960
This is...

13:49.850 --> 13:53.410
This is trash game bullshit!

13:53.410 --> 13:54.940
Going around half-naked?

13:54.940 --> 13:55.460
So lame!

13:55.460 --> 13:56.650
Couldn't be me.

13:56.650 --> 13:57.810
What a freak!

13:57.810 --> 13:58.940
Is it a reference to something?

14:00.530 --> 14:02.240
Calm down, Sunraku.

14:02.240 --> 14:05.070
Remember the three principles 
you learned from trash games:

14:06.570 --> 14:07.910
Patient mind.

14:09.120 --> 14:10.700
Unbreakable spirit.

14:12.240 --> 14:15.500
And cool-headed judgment.

14:15.830 --> 14:16.500
<i><b>Sunraku</b></i>

14:15.850 --> 14:16.500
<b>Mercenary (Twin Blade User)  Skill Points Remaining: 50</b>

14:17.930 --> 14:23.380
Looks like you rack up a lot of experience 
from just fighting a unique monster...

14:19.500 --> 14:23.380
<i><b>Sunraku</b></i>

14:19.500 --> 14:23.380
<b>Mercenary (Twin Blade User)  Skill Points Remaining: 50</b>

14:19.500 --> 14:23.380
<b>Cash on Hand            9000 Mahni</b>

14:24.120 --> 14:25.560
Which means I leveled up quite a bit,

14:25.560 --> 14:28.870
buffed up my skills and got lots 
of stat points to allocate!

14:29.260 --> 14:32.890
This might be a good time to define my build.

14:32.890 --> 14:37.520
I'd better distribute these 
fifty points carefully.

14:40.740 --> 14:42.730
Vitality, 6.

14:41.860 --> 14:43.110
<b>Redo</b>

14:43.100 --> 14:46.540
I made myself a glass cannon 
who can die in one hit!

14:46.540 --> 14:47.740
But what else could I do?!

14:47.740 --> 14:50.370
I'm locked out of two out 
of four of my armor slots!

14:50.370 --> 14:52.990
Spending points on vitality 
is like pissing in the ocean!

14:52.990 --> 14:54.350
Same with my HP!

14:54.350 --> 14:57.000
I'm just gonna have to cover 
with speed and stamina!

14:57.430 --> 15:00.830
And my best stat is a 65 in luck...

15:01.910 --> 15:04.170
The reason I got off then 
with one HP remaining...

15:04.810 --> 15:08.660
That's gotta be my luck at play... right?

15:10.100 --> 15:11.740
It's gotta do something, right?

15:12.580 --> 15:16.680
Yeah, I mean... I've been through 
enough hell already, right?

15:16.920 --> 15:20.690
It's okay to turn to luck for help, right?!

15:21.980 --> 15:22.650
Ow!

15:25.150 --> 15:26.320
What now?!

15:28.520 --> 15:29.440
What's a rabbit doing...

15:29.920 --> 15:31.320
I-Is that...

15:31.450 --> 15:32.450
<b>Vorpal Bunny</b>

15:31.720 --> 15:33.130
a Vorpal Bunny?!

15:34.050 --> 15:35.300
It is, right?

15:35.300 --> 15:37.040
Though, it doesn't look quite the same...

15:37.580 --> 15:40.890
Hang on, does this game let 
monsters spawn in towns?!

15:44.330 --> 15:46.000
Get back here, you!

15:51.910 --> 15:53.910
No, that outfit it's wearing...

15:53.910 --> 15:55.970
That's not just some Vorpal Bunny!

15:59.000 --> 16:02.270
I bet if I catch it, I'll get a rare item!

16:02.270 --> 16:04.170
It's gotta be that kind of thing!

16:09.350 --> 16:11.570
Yes! I got you!

16:15.420 --> 16:16.450
A door?

16:27.090 --> 16:29.050
Unique Scenario
<b>Invitation from Rabituza</b>

16:29.980 --> 16:31.090
What the...

16:31.640 --> 16:34.420
"Unique Scenario: Invitation from Rabituza"?

16:34.790 --> 16:37.780
I get it. I saw this on 
the game guide site...

16:37.780 --> 16:38.600
I think...

16:39.240 --> 16:43.820
"<i>SLF</i> has a sweeping main story 
about the exploration of the world,

16:43.820 --> 16:47.640
<i>but it's also got a huge 
number of side quests.</i>

16:47.640 --> 16:50.500
<i>One subset of these is 
called 'unique scenarios,'</i>

16:50.500 --> 16:53.910
<i>mystery scenarios whose 
unlock times, locations,</i>

16:53.910 --> 16:58.240
<i>contents, and flags aren't publicly known."</i>

16:58.810 --> 17:03.750
<i>"So the equipment, skills, and spells you 
can acquire in these unique scenarios...</i>

17:02.400 --> 17:03.750
What the heck is this?

17:03.750 --> 17:07.250
<i>...are said to all be top-class."</i>

17:07.680 --> 17:12.490
<i>So it's not unusual to see clans 
searching desperately to find</i>

17:12.490 --> 17:14.680
<i>these unique scenarios, huh?</i>

17:16.710 --> 17:19.540
To encounter one this 
early in my playthrough...

17:19.540 --> 17:22.700
Is this the result of dumping 
my stat points into luck?!

17:22.700 --> 17:24.790
I won't let this chance slip away!

17:26.770 --> 17:32.280
Unique Scenario
<b>Invitation from Rabituza</b>

17:30.130 --> 17:32.280
Rec. Level               <b>80</b>

17:32.280 --> 17:34.780
Rec. Level  <b>80</b>

17:34.840 --> 17:40.280
<b><i>Sunraku LV:28</i></b>

17:40.780 --> 17:44.290
<b>Rabituza</b>

17:50.670 --> 17:56.110
Wh-What is this place?!

18:02.570 --> 18:04.100
Everywhere I look...

18:04.860 --> 18:06.700
It's Vorpal Bunnies?!

18:08.110 --> 18:10.520
Did I end up in a monsters' lair?

18:11.380 --> 18:13.700
My fondest welcomes to you, Sunraku-san!

18:14.070 --> 18:16.290
I've <i>dearly</i> wanted to meet you!

18:18.650 --> 18:20.950
What?! Hello?!

18:21.930 --> 18:25.190
All of Rabituza is abuzz about you, you know!

18:25.190 --> 18:27.210
Despite your great personal weakness,

18:27.210 --> 18:29.920
you had the courage to attempt 
the Nightslayer all on your own!

18:29.920 --> 18:35.220
And the skills to continue striking perfect 
deadly blows without taking a single hit...!

18:35.220 --> 18:38.720
You are the embodiment of the vorpal soul!

18:38.960 --> 18:40.590
V-Vorpal soul?

18:40.880 --> 18:42.830
If only I could be like you!

18:42.830 --> 18:46.030
B-But I barely left a scratch on the thing...

18:46.030 --> 18:48.530
Only because it's so very, very powerful!

18:48.530 --> 18:49.950
The Night Emperor is a Colossus,

18:49.950 --> 18:52.730
capable of gobbling down 
wyverns like a midday snack!

18:53.070 --> 18:55.970
That you are even here 
speaking to me now suggests

18:55.970 --> 18:59.360
you are one of the pioneers 
under the Divinity's protection!

18:57.730 --> 18:59.350
<i>Boy, this bunny loves to talk...</i>

18:59.350 --> 19:02.020
And those marks upon your body prove that

19:02.020 --> 19:04.640
the Night Emperor regards 
you not as mere prey,

19:04.640 --> 19:07.220
but as a fellow being!

19:07.220 --> 19:08.960
How amazing!

19:08.960 --> 19:12.010
<i>It's not the first game I've 
played where the monsters talk...</i>

19:12.010 --> 19:14.100
<i>Is this thing an NPC?</i>

19:14.100 --> 19:16.630
<i>It seems pretty focused on Lycagon...</i>

19:16.840 --> 19:19.130
<i>Actually, that one trait of the Mark...</i>

19:20.380 --> 19:22.240
Conversations with NPCs will be affected by
the presence of Lycagon's Mark

19:22.390 --> 19:24.760
<i>Is this what it was talking about?</i>

19:24.760 --> 19:27.680
And in light of your great 
deeds, my Da— ahem—

19:27.680 --> 19:30.030
our boss would very much 
like to speak with you,

19:30.030 --> 19:32.270
hence why I was sent to fetch you!

19:32.880 --> 19:34.690
M-Meet me?

19:35.020 --> 19:39.570
I hope this isn't revenge for all the 
Vorpal Bunnies I killed, Miss, um...

19:39.570 --> 19:40.320
Oh!

19:40.890 --> 19:43.570
You may call me Emul!

19:48.120 --> 19:50.610
<i>Is this thing really AI?</i>

19:50.610 --> 19:52.910
<i>It can even guess what I was gonna ask...</i>

19:52.910 --> 19:54.930
You may rest easy, I assure you.

19:54.930 --> 19:58.170
Our boss is <i>far</i> above petty 
matters like revenge.

20:04.470 --> 20:07.470
<b>Palace of
Rabituza</b>

20:14.250 --> 20:16.240
Look at that craftsmanship!

20:16.240 --> 20:19.730
Quite a number of humans visit Rabituza,

20:19.730 --> 20:23.950
but you'll be the first 
one to visit the palace!

20:23.950 --> 20:25.210
The first one?!

20:25.870 --> 20:27.490
Does that mean...

20:27.950 --> 20:31.370
Is this a unique scenario only I know about?!

20:31.860 --> 20:35.810
When that piece of crap dog gave me 
this Mark, I was pretty worried...

20:36.500 --> 20:39.230
But it looks like my luck's 
finally turned around!

20:39.230 --> 20:41.800
Come, come! Right this way!

20:46.140 --> 20:47.540
Daddy—

20:47.540 --> 20:49.010
I mean, Boss!

20:49.230 --> 20:53.210
I brought the human bearer of 
the vorpal soul to see you!

20:53.920 --> 20:56.000
What kind of show of gratitude—

21:13.320 --> 21:15.230
Took you long enough.

21:16.060 --> 21:21.550
So, you're the one that pup beat
up and took a piss on?

21:21.550 --> 21:23.040
Y-Yeah...

21:23.040 --> 21:23.920
Go on!

21:23.920 --> 21:27.930
You people lose your vorpal soul so quickly.

21:28.190 --> 21:32.130
I'd assumed you were all hopeless, but...

21:32.130 --> 21:34.310
Looks like at least one 
of you's got some promise.

21:41.610 --> 21:43.000
Well?

21:43.000 --> 21:46.820
Mind giving me a bit of your time?

21:54.430 --> 21:57.600
I'm the boss here in Rabituza.

21:57.600 --> 22:00.190
The name's Vysache.

22:00.400 --> 22:04.960
Boss of Rabituza
<b>Vysache</b>

23:41.940 --> 23:49.200
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:42.630 --> 23:46.480
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:45.750 --> 23:49.190
<i><b>Psyger: Episode-0</b></i>

23:46.480 --> 23:47.930
Mini!

23:51.200 --> 23:58.200
<b>Time Chaser 2
 Bullets of Amber</b>

23:51.530 --> 23:55.290
This game is really hard for me.

23:55.290 --> 23:57.840
But if I can't finish it,

23:58.200 --> 24:04.810
I p-probably won't be able to go on an 
adventure with Hizutome-kun... right?

24:05.220 --> 24:09.690
Listen, I think you get good 
at games impressively quickly.

24:09.690 --> 24:14.720
but instead of these niche games, you might 
want to play one with broader appeal.

24:14.720 --> 24:16.800
B-But...

24:16.800 --> 24:20.800
It's Hizutome's skill levels 
that make him such a frea—

24:20.800 --> 24:23.620
er, such a unique individual.

24:23.620 --> 24:26.750
I understand that you don't 
want to hold him back,

24:26.750 --> 24:29.540
but maybe you should work 
on your fundamentals.

24:29.900 --> 24:31.990
Fundamentals?

24:31.990 --> 24:37.110
The truth is, there's a game that unique 
individual will definitely try out!

24:37.110 --> 24:38.080
What is it?!

24:38.740 --> 24:41.610
The polar opposite of the 
trash games. The god game!

24:41.610 --> 24:46.920
With over 30 million players 
worldwide, it's <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>?

24:47.220 --> 24:49.110
<i>SLF</i> for short, right?

24:49.570 --> 24:50.770
I've heard of it.

24:50.770 --> 24:52.580
My sister's really into it.

24:53.420 --> 24:55.930
What if you have your 
sister teach you the game,

24:55.930 --> 24:59.600
and become strong enough that you 
can show Hizutome-kun the ropes?

25:00.050 --> 25:01.080
Show him the ropes?

25:02.080 --> 25:04.440
Th-That's a good idea!

25:04.440 --> 25:06.310
Thanks for coming!

25:09.970 --> 25:14.790
I'm going to become strong enough 
to show Hizutome-kun the ropes!

25:15.330 --> 25:16.970
<i>What Mana didn't realize</i>

25:16.970 --> 25:19.670
<i>was that her advice, offered 
in a spirit of friendship,</i>

25:19.670 --> 25:24.790
<i>would create a hopeless 
addict in <i>SLF</i>'s world.</i>
